            "reasoning": "Let me analyze the requirements carefully.\n\nI need to write ONE new file: `docs/PLUMBLINE-ORCHESTRATOR-FIELD-GUIDE.md`.\n\nRequirements:\n(a) status line near top: non-normative, doctrine wins\n(b) reflects Owner decisions of 2026-10-28 15:52 EDT:\n   - tripwire at exactly 3 of the same failure class, then change the request\n   - shared key behind harness pre-call spend guard, key-usage reconciliation an upper bound (do not recommend a per-job key)\n   - cross-family pre-read optional, decided per job on the approval sheet\n(c) keeps these rules:\n   - finish_reason length with empty content is its own failure class (stop at first one)\n   - no throttling (endpoint max output, no reasoning limit), sized tasks, finish_reason logged on every call\n   - cap counts E-DI iterations\n   - handoffs name the command that writes files\n   - check handoffs against standing rules\n   - live test of each model instrument is a freeze gate\n   - write-once evidence\n   - relayed approvals are not approvals\n   - no /tmp\n(d) every rule paired with its real story (concrete incident from a real job or review, taken from drafts), placed with rule, field-guide style\n(e) no verbatim quotes of Owner (paraphrase Owner decisions as Owner decisions); no personal names, no email addresses, no absolute local paths, no key material or key fingerprints. Model and org names drafts cite are fine.\n(f) stale open items become a short list under heading containing \"Carried forward\"\nExpect ~15 KB.\n\nNow the G5-G7 checks:\n\nG5: One of first 15 lines contains `status`, `non-normative`, `doctrine wins`.\n\nG6 groups:\n- B1: `same failure class` + `3 times`/`three times`/`third time` + `change the request`\n- B2: `shared key` + `spend guard` + `upper bound`\n- B3: `pre-read` + `optional` + `approval sheet`\n- C1: `finish_reason` + `length` + `empty content` + `own failure class`\n- C2: `no throttling` + `endpoint max` + `reasoning limit`\n- C3: `size each task`/`size