iting \"key ... hash ... hex\". Actually this regex: `key` then within 24 chars `fingerprint|sha256|sha-256|hash`, then within 12 chars 8+ hex digits. So I should avoid any sentence like \"key hash 708359c6\". I'll just avoid mentioning key fingerprints entirely. But careful with words like \"key\" followed by \"hash\". Let me avoid combining \"key\" and \"hash\" near hex. Actually simpler: avoid hex strings ≥8 chars anywhere near \"key\". Hmm, also \"sha256\" near \"key\". Let me just not include any long hex strings at all. The drafts have things like `b8fef62` (7 chars), `067c524` (7 chars), `708359c6…9bcb` (8+ hex). Avoid those. Use commit references sparingly without hashes, or 7-char hashes are fine (7 hex < 8). Actually \"8 or more\" — 7 chars is safe. But better to avoid entirely.\n\nAlso deny_phrases: 28 phrases, matched after normalization and dropping non-letter/digit/space characters. So I must not include those phrases. Let me list them and make sure I paraphrase:\n\n1. \"Ratified proceed\"\n2. \"I agree with all of these\"\n3. \"Item 29 - (A) approved as recommended\"\n4. \"Item 28 - (B) fix it in this job\"\n5. \"Remaining - (A) approved as recommended\"\n6. \"Adopt the tripwire: after the same Maker failure 3 times, stop and change the request\"\n7. \"Keep the shared key with the spend guard\"\n8. \"Make the cross-family pre-read optional, decided per job\"\n9. \"Use the same openrouter key I gave you last time\"\n10. \"Item 30: the Maker writes the field guide in this job, with bar checks for it\"\n11. \"Paraphrase my words as Owner decisions; no verbatim quotes in the doc\"\n12. \"When I said three iterations, I was talking about three iterations of the EDI loop\"\n13. \"Looks like you choked the evaluator model\"\n14. \"don't put your work in /tmp\"\n15. \"As Owner I give disposition: accepted\"\n16. \"stop choking the model\"\n17. \"run the controls and instrument from a writable copy of freeze/ with byte-identical, hash-verified files\"\n18. \"I