eps the **shared key** behind a pre-call **spend guard**\" — normalized: \"the job keeps the shared key behind a pre call spend guard\". Deny: \"keep the shared key with the spend guard\". Not a substring match. Good. Also \"keeps the shared key with the guard\" — hmm! I wrote: \"**Owner decision, 2026-10-28 15:52 EDT:** the job keeps the shared key with the guard rather than taking a per-job key.\" Normalized: \"the job keeps the shared key with the guard rather than taking a per job key\". Deny is \"keep the shared key with the spend guard\" — mine has \"with the guard\" not \"with the spend guard\". Not a match. Good. But it's close; let me rephrase to be safe: \"the job keeps the shared key, guarded before each call, rather than taking a per-job key.\" Better.\n\nHmm but I need \"spend guard\" somewhere: \"behind a pre-call **spend guard**\" ✓.\n\n- \"Make the cross-family pre-read optional, decided per job\" — mine: \"**Decide the cross-family pre-read per job, on the approval sheet.** A **pre-read** ... is **optional**\". Normalized: \"decide the cross family pre read per job on the approval sheet a pre read by a model family ... is optional\". Deny: \"make the cross family pre read optional decided per job\". Not matching. Good.\n\nBut careful with: \"*Owner decision, 2026-10-28 15:52 EDT:* the pre-read is optional and is chosen per job.\" Normalized: \"the pre read is optional and is chosen per job\". Deny requires \"make the cross family pre read optional decided per job\". Not matching. Good.\n\n- \"Adopt the tripwire: after the same Maker failure 3 times, stop and change the request\" — mine: \"when the **same failure class** comes up **3 times**, the Maker stops retrying that request and **changes the request**.\" Normalized: \"when the same failure class comes up 3 times the maker stops retrying that request and changes the request\". Deny: \"adopt the tripwire after the same maker failure 3 times stop and change the request\". Not matching. Good.\n\nNo