"hash\" ... then hex. Not triggered. Good. But what about the deny regex applied to normalized lowercase text? \"2026 10 28\" has spaces, breaking the 8-run. Fine anyway.\n\nAlso I should double check: is there any 8+ hex string? \"NOT-CHECKABLE\" no. \"131,072\" no.\n\nNow, \"no absolute local paths\" — I use `dot-plumbline/jobs/<job_id>/` (relative), `custody/MANIFEST.sha256` (relative), `evidence/<name>-<hash8>.<ext>` (relative). Good.\n\nHmm, `<hash8>` — is that \"key fingerprint\"? No.\n\nNow, requirement (e): \"no personal names\". I mention no names. Model names: GLM? I don't actually name GLM. The drafts cite it. Should I name model families? \"E-GLM\" is an evaluator label. I'll mention \"a GLM-family judge\" maybe. Not necessary. I'll keep \"the model judge\". Maybe mention \"evaluatordriven\" as org/project — that's fine and cited.\n\nHmm, \"GrokBot\" — avoid.\n\nLet me also make sure J3: doesn't contradict Owner decisions. Check: \"no per-job-key recommendation\" — I explicitly say this guide does not recommend a per-job key. Good.\n\nOne risk: J3 says the guide must not claim to override the doctrine. My status line says \"where this guide and the doctrine disagree, the doctrine wins\". Good. Also add somewhere: \"Nothing here amends the bar or the doctrine.\"\n\nAlso J4 wants stories for every rule from (b) and (c). Let me double-check each (c) rule has a story:\n1. finish_reason length + empty content own failure class, stop at first → story (12-record, five retries). ✓\n2. no throttling (endpoint max, no reasoning limit) → story 1 & 2. ✓\n3. sized tasks → story (12 records, batching). ✓\n4. finish_reason logged on every call → hmm, needs a story. The 12-record story is the same, and \"the guarded harness already logs finish; keep it that way\". I have that in item 2. Let me make sure the story is attached: yes, item 2 includes the 12-record story and says the log shows a starved call. Also I can add: \"Ours: the guarded harness logged `finish` = `stop` with token counts on iteration 1, which is how we knew a call had room.\" Good, adds concreteness.\n5. cap counts E-DI iterations → story (cap 3 generations, AMENDMENT). ✓\n6. handoffs name the command that writes files → story (extract_files --check). ✓\n7. check handoffs against standing rules → story (helper handoff capped retries at one, committed as Owner). ✓\n8. live test of each model instrument is a freeze gate → story (64/64 dry run, splitter not live, five paid calls failed). ✓\n9. write-once evidence → story (emitter rewrites logs in place; tests change fixture logs). ✓\n10. relayed approvals are not approvals → story (seats' go-aheads logged as relays; one decision unattributable). ✓\n11. no /tmp → story (reboot wiped /tmp). ✓\n\n(b) three Owner decisions each with story ✓.\n\nGood.\n\nNow let me also make sure the doc is roughly 15 KB and reads like a field guide.\n\nOne more: G6 B3 requires \"approval sheet\" — I have it. Also I use \"sheet\" elsewhere.\n\nLet me also double check \"endpoint max\" — I wrote \"**endpoint max**\" in item 1. ✓ Normalized \"endpoint max\". Good.\n\nCheck \"no throttling\" — item 1 heading \"**No throttling.**\" → normalized \"no throttling\". ✓\n\nCheck \"own failure class\" — item 3: \"is its own failure class\". Normalized \"is its own failure class\" contains \"own failure class\" ✓.\n\nCheck \"empty content\" — item 3: \"with empty content\" ✓.\n\nCheck \"finish_reason\" — written with underscore; normalize drops `_` → \"finishreason\". Hmm!! The normalize rule drops `_`. So \"finish_reason\" → \"finishreason\". And the anchor in fg_rules is \"finish_reason\" — which would also be normalized to \"finishreason\" by the same rule. Presumably the anchors are normalized too. The spec says \"Phrase matching works on the normalized text\" and the anchors published in fg_rules.json are presumably normalized the same way before matching. So \"finish_reason\" in the doc → \"finishreason\" and anchor \"finish_reason\" → \"fin